				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lt-flops" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1735419); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1735419&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200817" alt="Lt Flops" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1735419)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lt-flops" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1735419); return false;" >Lt Flops</a></span> <span class="odate time_1561442453 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 Jun 2019 06:00</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4290504">
									

<p><strong>EDIT &#8212; September 8:</strong> In hindsight, I was being too hard on this article. There's nothing <em>wrong</em> here aside from my few quibbles about the use of the Shark Punching Centre. In fact, there's some great content here! This Centre-Pattern Screamer collaboration is very unique. So, take my following thoughts with a grain of salt.</p>
<hr />
<p>I will admit that the <em>only</em> thing holding me back from upvoting is the Centre's placement into the mainline SCP universe, but with neither an in-universe nor out-of-universe justification for that.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Thoughts</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Forgive me if this feedback becomes too heavy-handed.</p>
<p>So that I don't bury the lede: I enjoyed the &quot;weaponized pattern screamer whalesong&quot; concept. This team's writing achieves hilarious shenanigans in a proper clinical tone. But one thing the article flat-out ignores is that the SPC is almost exclusively, and rather explicitly, an alt-universe Group of Interest. Apart from &quot;they punch sharks&quot;, their alt-universe nature and the unique identity that stems from it is the only thing that keeps them cohesive and consistent. And I think it's a mistake to ignore that.</p>
<p>Shark Punching Center cameos used to be a throwaway joke. The premise was simple: sharks exist, and this bizarro Foundation is devoting their entire existence to punching them. And it got written like that for a while because it was funny. But over time &#8212; frankly? The joke got stale.</p>
<p>A few years ago, the GOI took a sharp turn into &quot;alt-universe&quot; territory. The SPC was transformed from &quot;silly people doing silly things&quot; into &quot;serious people being forced to deal with a silly world&quot; &#8212; where everyone is one punch away from completely losing their shit at the absurdity of their existence. And the concept benefitted immensely from that evolution. When I think of SPC, that's precisely what I imagine, and I think that transformation was when the SPC became a fresh new thing with its own identity.</p>
<p>I'll admit &#8212; it's silly that someone would so fervently argue against &quot;there is no canon&quot; for something so ridiculous as the SPC. Maybe I'm just being pedantic for opposing this. And I'm not even fully <em>against</em> writing an interaction between the Foundation and the Centre; hell, last year, I helped write exactly that, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/bird">with not_a_seagull (as above) and a couple of other writers</a>.</p>
<p><strong>TLDR:</strong> I guess what I'm trying to say here is. I dislike that the SPC's depiction here is inconsistent with other modern SPC articles. Don't get me wrong, this article is decently written, and it emulates classic SPC shenanigans and professional Foundation tone well on their own separate merits. But it would have a much better grip on its concepts if it relied on the stronger core a contemporary SPC has to offer. I hope this makes sense; no vote for now.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

